{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>For I cannot rise before you.</b> This indicates that before the giving of the Torah the ancients observed the laws of impurity regarding a menstruating woman and held her in impurity like the impurity of a corpse, as our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said in tractate Niddah: it is forbidden to inquire after the well-being of a niddah; Rabbi Nehemiah says, even the speech that proceeds from her mouth is impure; and it is forbidden to tread upon her dust, for she is impure like a corpse; and it is forbidden to benefit from the work of her hands. Therefore Laban fell silent and did not speak with her at all."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:45.128488964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}